The overall process of purchasing, obtaining FDA approval and the bypassing of FDA regulations.This is going to be several paragraphs.
Per the article Texas is currently experiencing a shortage of the state's execution drug, pentobarbital. Texas utilizes a compounding pharmacy which is not subject to FDA regulations to obtain the drug, from a European manufacturer, who has explicitly banned the use of their product in executions (1). According to the article Life Matters, "compounding pharmacies are not required to follow current Good Pharmacy Practices (cGMP) or FDA'', furthermore "The US Food and Drug Administration is not listed as a review or regulatory agency for compounding pharmacy reviews" (2).In 2015 Oklahoma used midazolam as a substitute for pentobarbital as part of a three-drug cocktail in an execution that went awry, the\\"
